@startuml order-state
title Order lifecycle (State pattern: domain/orders/states.py)
skinparam shadowing false
hide empty description

state "PendingPayment\n(pending_payment)" as PendingPayment
state "Accepted\n(accepted)" as Accepted
state "Preparing\n(preparing)" as Preparing
state "ReadyForPickup\n(ready_for_pickup)" as ReadyForPickup
state "Delivering\n(delivering)" as Delivering
state "Delivered\n(delivered)" as Delivered
state "Cancelled\n(cancelled)" as Cancelled

[*] --> PendingPayment : place order\n[online payment]
[*] --> Accepted : place order\n[cash]

PendingPayment --> Accepted : pay\n(payment verified)
Accepted --> Preparing : start_preparing\n(admin)
Preparing --> ReadyForPickup : mark_ready\n(admin)
ReadyForPickup --> Delivering : pick_up\n[courier order]\n(assigned courier)
ReadyForPickup --> Delivered : deliver\n[pickup order]\n(admin)
Delivering --> Delivered : deliver\n(assigned courier)

PendingPayment --> Cancelled : cancel\n(customer / admin)
Accepted --> Cancelled : cancel\n(customer / admin,\nrefund + points back)

Delivered --> [*]
Cancelled --> [*]

note right of ReadyForPickup
  A courier first "takes" the order
  (assigns themselves); the status
  stays ready_for_pickup until pick_up.
  pick_up stores the OSRM route
  and picked_up_at.
end note

note bottom of Delivered
  LoyaltyObserver credits bonus points;
  cash orders are marked paid.
end note

note "Any other action raises\nInvalidTransitionError → HTTP 409" as N1
@enduml
